{"text": "blueprint:\n  name: FLARE\n  description: >\n    FLARE: phase-based circadian lighting - sets brightness/colour\n    temperature from a FLARE schedule sensor,\n    keeping lights updated as it changes, and turns them off a while\n    after occupancy clears. Full details on every input:\n    [the blueprint reference](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/).\n\n\n    Blueprint version 0.0.0-dev - the integration raises a repair when a\n    newer one is available.\n  domain: automation\n  author: Dan Spencer\n  homeassistant:\n    # Required by the occupancy.* triggers/conditions.\n    min_version: 2026.11.0\n  input:\n    schedule:\n      name: Schedule\n      description: >\n        The FLARE schedule the room follows: the brightness and colour\n        temperature it applies.\n        [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n      selector:\n        device:\n          filter:\n            - integration: flare\n              model: Schedule\n    room_target:\n      name: Lights & Occupancy\n      description: >\n        Entity, device, area, floor, or label - lights within it are\n        controlled, occupancy and motion sensors within it decide when. Use\n        Exclude target to leave out sensors you don't want.\n        [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#room).\n      selector:\n        target:\n          entity:\n            - domain: light\n            - domain: binary_sensor\n              device_class: occupancy\n            - domain: binary_sensor\n              device_class: motion\n            - domain: sensor\n              device_class: illuminance\n    # A heading, not a setting: a constant with a blank label shows only its name and description.\n    customise_divider:\n      name: Customise\n      description: >\n        Which lights stay off, idle brightness and scenes, for each phase.\n        Use Custom when you need more control than per phase allows.\n      default: true\n      selector:\n        constant:\n          value: true\n          label: \" \"\n    morning_phase:\n      name: Morning\n      icon: mdi:weather-sunset-up\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        morning_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off\n          description: Lights in the room that stay off during Morning.\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        morning_idle_brightness:\n          name: Idle Brightness\n          description: >\n            The brightness (0-255) the room dims to when it's empty, instead\n            of switching off. Useful as a nightlight. Only works in rooms with\n            occupancy or motion sensors.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#idle-brightness).\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        morning_scene:\n          name: Scene\n          description: >\n            This scene is applied during the phase. Any lights not in it stay\n            on the schedule.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#scenes).\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n    day_phase:\n      name: Day\n      icon: mdi:white-balance-sunny\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        day_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off\n          description: Lights in the room that stay off during Day.\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        day_idle_brightness:\n          name: Idle Brightness\n          description: >\n            The brightness (0-255) the room dims to when it's empty, instead\n            of switching off. Useful as a nightlight. Only works in rooms with\n            occupancy or motion sensors.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#idle-brightness).\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        day_scene:\n          name: Scene\n          description: >\n            This scene is applied during the phase. Any lights not in it stay\n            on the schedule.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#scenes).\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n    evening_phase:\n      name: Evening\n      icon: mdi:weather-sunset-down\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        evening_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off\n          description: Lights in the room that stay off during Evening.\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        evening_idle_brightness:\n          name: Idle Brightness\n          description: >\n            The brightness (0-255) the room dims to when it's empty, instead\n            of switching off. Useful as a nightlight. Only works in rooms with\n            occupancy or motion sensors.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#idle-brightness).\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        evening_scene:\n          name: Scene\n          description: >\n            This scene is applied during the phase. Any lights not in it stay\n            on the schedule.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#scenes).\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n    night_phase:\n      name: Night\n      icon: mdi:weather-night\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        night_exclude_lights:\n          name: Lights Off\n          description: Lights in the room that stay off during Night.\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: light\n              multiple: true\n          default: []\n        night_idle_brightness:\n          name: Idle Brightness\n          description: >\n            The brightness (0-255) the room dims to when it's empty, instead\n            of switching off. Useful as a nightlight. Only works in rooms with\n            occupancy or motion sensors.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#idle-brightness).\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 255\n              mode: box\n        night_scene:\n          name: Scene\n          description: >\n            This scene is applied during the phase. Any lights not in it stay\n            on the schedule.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#scenes).\n          default: null\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              domain: scene\n    templates:\n      name: Custom\n      icon: mdi:code-braces\n      description: >\n        Templates for when per-phase settings aren't enough, like dimming the\n        room while the TV is on. Whenever a template returns a value, it\n        overrides the per-phase setting.\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        brightness_template:\n          name: Brightness Template\n          description: >\n            Returns each light's brightness, 0-255, in place of the\n            schedule's: {{ {'light.lamp': 50} }}. '50%' is a percentage of\n            full brightness, and 'x0.5' multiplies the schedule's. 0 switches\n            a light off; null leaves it alone. When it returns a light, its value overrides\n            Lights Off for that light.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#brightness-template).\n          default: \"{{ {} }}\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        idle_brightness_template:\n          name: Idle Brightness Template\n          description: >\n            Returns the brightness (1-255, or a percentage like '5%') each\n            light dims to when the room is empty: {{ {'light.lamp': 10} }}.\n            When it returns a light, its value\n            overrides Idle Brightness for that light. Only works in rooms with\n            occupancy or motion sensors.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#idle-brightness).\n          default: \"{{ {} }}\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        scene_template:\n          name: Scene Template\n          description: >\n            Returns a scene to use instead of the schedule, or nothing to\n            carry on as normal. When it returns one, it overrides the phase's\n            Scene.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#scenes).\n          default: \"\"\n          selector:\n            template: {}\n        additional_triggers:\n          name: Additional Triggers\n          description: >\n            Update the room straight away when one of these fires, like the\n            TV starting to play or an entity a template reads changing. They\n            only adjust lights that are already on.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#additional-triggers).\n          default: []\n          selector:\n            trigger: {}\n    # A heading, like customise_divider.\n    advanced_divider:\n      name: Fine Tuning\n      description: When the room reacts, and how. The defaults suit most rooms.\n      default: true\n      selector:\n        constant:\n          value: true\n          label: \" \"\n    sensors:\n      name: Sensors & Conditions\n      icon: mdi:motion-sensor\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        no_motion_wait:\n          name: Wait Time\n          description: >\n            How long every occupancy and motion sensor must be clear before\n            the room counts as empty and its lights turn off.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#wait-time).\n          default: 120\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 3600\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n        lux_threshold:\n          name: Lux Threshold\n          description: >\n            Above this many lux on every illuminance sensor, the room stays\n            dark. If someone's still there when it gets darker, the lights\n            come on then. Switching the room on by hand still works. 0 turns\n            this off.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#lux-threshold).\n          default: 0\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 2000\n              step: 10\n              unit_of_measurement: lx\n        conditions:\n          name: Conditions\n          description: >\n            If any are set, the room only updates while all of them are true.\n            The rest of the time it's paused and leaves the lights alone.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#conditions).\n          default: []\n          selector:\n            condition: {}\n    timing:\n      name: Transitions\n      icon: mdi:timer-outline\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        motion_on_transition:\n          name: Turning On\n          description: How long lights take to fade up when someone arrives or the room is switched on.\n          default: 1\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n        motion_off_transition:\n          name: Turning Off\n          description: How long lights take to fade out once the room is empty.\n          default: 15\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n        background_transition:\n          name: Everything Else\n          description: How long other changes take to fade in, like the schedule moving on or a template changing. Nobody is waiting on these.\n          default: 5\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 0\n              max: 60\n              unit_of_measurement: seconds\n    settings:\n      name: Other Settings\n      icon: mdi:cog-outline\n      collapsed: true\n      input:\n        override_protection:\n          name: Override Protection\n          description: >\n            Leaves a light alone once something else changes it, until all of\n            the room's lights are off. Turn it off for a room whose bulbs report\n            something other than what they show.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#override-protection).\n          default: true\n          selector:\n            boolean:\n        rgb_phases:\n          name: Prefer RGB During\n          description: >\n            Phases that send RGB colour rather than colour temperature to\n            lights that support it. Cool whites can look blue in RGB, so\n            Morning and Day are off by default.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#prefer-rgb-during).\n          default: [Evening, Night]\n          selector:\n            select:\n              options: [Morning, Day, Evening, Night]\n              multiple: true\n        stored_traces:\n          name: Stored Traces\n          description: >\n            How many of the automation's recent runs to keep traces of. The\n            room updates every minute, so this is roughly how many minutes\n            back you can look.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#stored-traces).\n          default: 20\n          selector:\n            number:\n              min: 1\n              max: 200\n              mode: box\n        # Deprecated: removed in FLARE 3.0 (tests/checks/test_deprecated_inputs.py).\n        use_area_sensors:\n          name: Sensors From Areas (Deprecated)\n          description: >\n            Deprecated and will be removed as an option in FLARE 3.0: use\n            \"Exclude target\" in Lights & Occupancy instead of turning this\n            off. Only shown while it's off.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#sensors-from-areas).\n          # Shown only while it's off: hidden, an input reads as its\n          # default, so hiding it at the default can't change a room.\n          visible:\n            field: use_area_sensors\n            value: false\n          default: true\n          selector:\n            boolean: {}\n        # Deprecated: removed in FLARE 3.0 (tests/checks/test_deprecated_inputs.py).\n        extra_triggers:\n          name: Additional Trigger Entities (Deprecated)\n          description: >\n            Deprecated and will be removed as an option in FLARE 3.0: add a\n            State trigger to Additional Triggers instead. Entities that make\n            the room update as soon as they change.\n            [Details](https://danrspencer.github.io/flare/reference/blueprint/#additional-trigger-entities).\n          default: []\n          selector:\n            entity:\n              multiple: true\n\nmode: restart\nmax_exceeded: silent\ntrace:\n  stored_traces: !input stored_traces\n\n# Available to triggers and conditions, unlike variables:.\ntrigger_variables:\n  room_target: !input room_target\n  use_area_sensors: !input use_area_sensors\n  lux_threshold: !input lux_threshold\n  # The first area the room names, whose tick it follows; none if it names\n  # no area. Trigger templates can't look anything up, so only an area\n  # named directly counts.\n  tick_area: >-\n    {% set areas = room_target.area_id if room_target is mapping and room_target.area_id is defined else [] %}\n    {% set areas = [areas] if areas is string else (areas or []) %}\n    {{ areas | first if areas | length > 0 else none }}\n\ntrigger:\n  # The schedule's Phase, which fires on a real phase change (and once at\n  # startup), never on an attribute-only update.\n  - id: phase_change\n    trigger: event.received\n    target:\n      device_id: !input schedule\n    options:\n      event_type:\n        - Morning\n        - Day\n        - Evening\n        - Night\n  # The area's tick, spaced from every other area's. The curve is flat in\n  # Morning/Night, so phase_change goes quiet there. Also runs self-heal.\n  - id: tick\n    trigger: event\n    event_type: flare_tick\n    event_data:\n      area_id: \"{{ tick_area }}\"\n    enabled: \"{{ tick_area is not none }}\"\n  # A room naming no area ticks on the minute instead. Every such room\n  # writes in the same second, which is what area ticks spread out.\n  - id: tick\n    trigger: time_pattern\n    minutes: \"*\"\n    enabled: \"{{ tick_area is none }}\"\n  - id: extra\n    platform: state\n    entity_id: !input extra_triggers\n  # Occupancy and motion sensors share the ids. Harmless with no sensor of\n  # either kind in the room. With Sensors From Areas off, `condition:` drops\n  # those from sensors not picked by name.\n  - id: motion_on\n    trigger: occupancy.detected\n    target: !input room_target\n  - id: motion_on\n    trigger: motion.detected\n    target: !input room_target\n  - id: motion_off\n    trigger: occupancy.cleared\n    target: !input room_target\n    options:\n      for:\n        seconds: !input no_motion_wait\n  - id: motion_off\n    trigger: motion.cleared\n    target: !input room_target\n    options:\n      for:\n        seconds: !input no_motion_wait\n  - id: recovered\n    platform: template\n    value_template: >\n      {#\n        Runs an ordinary tick as soon as a light becomes reachable, rather\n        than waiting for the next one. \"At least one reachable\", not \"none\n        unavailable\", so a dead entity can't block it; a bulb recovering\n        beside reachable siblings waits for the tick. Can't use `trigger.*`,\n        which isn't in scope here. Held for a few seconds, so a bulb that has\n        just powered up has booted before it's sent anything.\n      #}\n      {% set ns = namespace(entities=[], devices=[], areas=[]) %}\n      {% for key in ['entity_id', 'device_id', 'area_id', 'floor_id', 'label_id'] %}\n        {% set v = room_target.get(key, []) %}\n        {% set ids = [v] if v is string else v %}\n        {% if key == 'entity_id' %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'device_id' %}{% set ns.devices = ns.devices + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'area_id' %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'floor_id' %}\n          {% for f in ids %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + floor_areas(f) %}{% endfor %}\n        {% else %}\n          {% for l in ids %}\n            {% set ns.entities = ns.entities + label_entities(l) %}\n            {% set ns.devices = ns.devices + label_devices(l) %}\n            {% set ns.areas = ns.areas + label_areas(l) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n        {% endif %}\n      {% endfor %}\n      {% for d in ns.devices %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + device_entities(d) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% for a in ns.areas %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + area_entities(a) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% set light_entity_ids = ns.entities | select('match', '^light\\\\.')\n           | reject('in', integration_entities('flare')) | unique | list %}\n      {{ light_entity_ids\n         | reject('is_state', 'unavailable') | reject('is_state', 'unknown')\n         | list | length > 0 }}\n    for:\n      seconds: 5\n\n  # The room stops being too bright for Lux Threshold, so it can light up for\n  # someone already there. Only a wake-up: the action re-checks both with the\n  # room as resolve_target finds it. Expands the target the same way as\n  # `recovered`; with Sensors From Areas off, only sensors picked by name.\n  - id: lux_dark\n    platform: template\n    value_template: >\n      {% set threshold = lux_threshold | float(0) %}\n      {% set ns = namespace(entities=[], devices=[], areas=[]) %}\n      {% for key in ['entity_id', 'device_id', 'area_id', 'floor_id', 'label_id'] %}\n        {% set v = room_target.get(key, []) %}\n        {% set ids = [v] if v is string else v %}\n        {% if key == 'entity_id' %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + ids %}\n        {% elif not use_area_sensors %}\n        {% elif key == 'device_id' %}{% set ns.devices = ns.devices + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'area_id' %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + ids %}\n        {% elif key == 'floor_id' %}\n          {% for f in ids %}{% set ns.areas = ns.areas + floor_areas(f) %}{% endfor %}\n        {% else %}\n          {% for l in ids %}\n            {% set ns.entities = ns.entities + label_entities(l) %}\n            {% set ns.devices = ns.devices + label_devices(l) %}\n            {% set ns.areas = ns.areas + label_areas(l) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n        {% endif %}\n      {% endfor %}\n      {% for d in ns.devices %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + device_entities(d) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% for a in ns.areas %}{% set ns.entities = ns.entities + area_entities(a) %}{% endfor %}\n      {% set lux = ns.entities | select('match', '^sensor\\\\.')\n           | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'illuminance') | unique\n           | map('states') | select('is_number') | map('float') | list %}\n      {{ threshold > 0\n         and not (lux | length > 0 and lux | select('le', threshold) | list | count == 0) }}\n\n  # The user's own triggers, last: one at position 10 or later is theirs,\n  # whatever its id (trigger_id below).\n  - triggers: !input additional_triggers\n\nvariables:\n  # Which trigger ran, by position for the user's own: an Additional Trigger\n  # is `additional` whatever id it was given, so one named motion_on can't\n  # light the room. 10 is how many triggers precede `additional_triggers`\n  # (tests/checks/test_blueprint_triggers.py). None for a manual run.\n  trigger_id: >-\n    {% if trigger is defined and trigger.idx is defined and trigger.idx | int(-1) >= 10 %}additional\n    {%- elif trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined %}{{ trigger.id }}\n    {%- else %}{{ none }}{% endif %}\n  schedule: !input schedule\n  # Who's writing, for override protection: this automation, or no one.\n  # The room's lights, released together, are resolved_entities.\n  override_protection_on: !input override_protection\n  room_id: \"{{ this.entity_id if override_protection_on else none }}\"\n  # The schedule device's one sensor, which carries the curve.\n  adaptive_sensor: >\n    {{ device_entities(schedule) | select('match', '^sensor\\\\.') | first | default(none) }}\n  scene_template: !input scene_template\n  background_transition: !input background_transition\n  motion_on_transition: !input motion_on_transition\n  no_motion_wait: !input no_motion_wait\n  lux_threshold: !input lux_threshold\n  rgb_phases: !input rgb_phases\n  phase: \"{{ states(adaptive_sensor) }}\"\n  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ phase in rgb_phases }}\"\n  script_transition: >\n    {# Slow for background updates; quick for motion or a manual run. #}\n    {% if trigger_id in ['phase_change', 'tick', 'extra', 'additional', 'recovered', 'lux_dark'] %}\n      {{ background_transition }}\n    {% else %}\n      {{ motion_on_transition }}\n    {% endif %}\n  # Nothing triggered this run: \"Run\" was pressed, or automation.trigger\n  # was called. Forces the tick through override protection.\n  manual_run: \"{{ not (trigger is defined and trigger.id is defined) }}\"\n  # Entities picked by name in Room Target, as written: the only sensors\n  # that count with Sensors From Areas off.\n  named_entities: >\n    {% set v = room_target.get('entity_id', []) %}\n    {{ [v] if v is string else v }}\n\n# Plain reading of the inputs, so it needs no resolve_target.\ncondition:\n  - alias: \"Not a sensor that Sensors From Areas leaves out\"\n    condition: template\n    value_template: >\n      {{ use_area_sensors or manual_run\n         or trigger_id not in ['motion_on', 'motion_off']\n         or trigger.entity_id in named_entities }}\n  # `and`, as an automation's own conditions are, so an empty list is met.\n  # automation.trigger skips conditions by default, so a manual run and a\n  # flare still get through.\n  - alias: \"The room's Conditions are met\"\n    condition: and\n    conditions: !input conditions\n\naction:\n  # Room Target as Home Assistant resolves it for an action, which is how a\n  # flare finds its lights too. Everything below works from it, so the\n  # variables that need it are set here rather than before the trigger's\n  # conditions.\n  - alias: \"Find the room's lights and sensors\"\n    action: flare.resolve_target\n    target: !input room_target\n    response_variable: room\n  - alias: \"Work out what the room needs\"\n    variables:\n      room_entities: \"{{ room.entities }}\"\n      # Not a flare's own light, which would pass the room's values on to\n      # every light in it as an override.\n      resolved_entities: >\n        {{ room_entities | select('match', '^light\\\\.')\n           | reject('in', integration_entities('flare')) | list }}\n      # The room's illuminance sensors, picked the same way as its occupancy\n      # ones: inferred from the target, or only those named with Sensors From\n      # Areas off. A sensor that isn't available or isn't numeric can't say\n      # how bright the room is, so it doesn't count.\n      room_lux_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(sensors=[]) %}\n        {% for e in room_entities | select('match', '^sensor\\\\.')\n             | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'illuminance') %}\n          {% if states(e) | is_number %}\n            {% set ns.sensors = ns.sensors + [e] %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.sensors if use_area_sensors\n           else ns.sensors | select('in', named_entities) | list }}\n      # Every illuminance sensor reading above the Lux Threshold: bright\n      # enough without the room's lights. 0 turns the check off, no sensor\n      # means nothing to go on, and a manual run (the Run button, the flare,\n      # a voice assistant) overrides it - this stops the automation lighting\n      # a bright room by itself, not someone asking for the lights.\n      too_bright: >\n        {% set threshold = lux_threshold | float(0) %}\n        {{ threshold > 0 and not manual_run\n           and room_lux_entities | length > 0\n           and room_lux_entities | map('states') | map('float', 0)\n               | select('le', threshold) | list | count == 0 }}\n      # Off lights stay off while it's too bright; ones already on are left\n      # in the call, so the curve keeps driving them.\n      lux_blocked_entities: >\n        {{ resolved_entities | reject('is_state', 'on') | list if too_bright else [] }}\n      # Up here because variables: render top to bottom and the turn-off lists\n      # below need it.\n      # Public: the templates read it, and the docs name it. None while the\n      # schedule is unavailable.\n      schedule_brightness: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'brightness') }}\"\n      template_brightness_levels: !input brightness_template\n      morning_exclude_lights: !input morning_exclude_lights\n      day_exclude_lights: !input day_exclude_lights\n      evening_exclude_lights: !input evening_exclude_lights\n      night_exclude_lights: !input night_exclude_lights\n      phase_exclude_lights: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_exclude_lights, 'Day': day_exclude_lights,\n                    'Evening': evening_exclude_lights, 'Night': night_exclude_lights} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase, []) }}\n      # The template overrides the per-phase exclude list. A single level from\n      # the template means every light in the room. '50%' and 'x0.5' are read\n      # by flare.apply_lighting.\n      template_brightness_map: >\n        {% set t = template_brightness_levels %}\n        {% set relative = t is string and (t | trim) is match('^([xX] *[0-9.]+|[0-9.]+ *%)$') %}\n        {% if t is mapping %}\n          {{ t }}\n        {% elif relative or (t is not none and (t | string | trim) != '' and (t | float(-1)) >= 0) %}\n          {% set level = (t | trim) if relative else (t | float) %}\n          {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: level}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n          {{ ns.m }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ {} }}\n        {% endif %}\n      brightness_levels: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% for e in phase_exclude_lights %}\n          {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: 0}) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ dict(ns.m, **template_brightness_map) }}\n      # Lights handed off with a null/false level (\"something else owns\n      # this\"), unlike 0 (\"turn off\"). `is sameas false`, since `0 == false`\n      # in Jinja. Excluded from the turn-offs too.\n      hands_off_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(items=[]) %}\n        {% for entity_id, level in brightness_levels.items() %}\n          {% if level is none or level is sameas false %}\n            {% set ns.items = ns.items + [entity_id] %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.items }}\n      color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'color_temp_kelvin') }}\"\n      # None while the sensor is unavailable.\n      rgb_color: \"{{ state_attr(adaptive_sensor, 'rgb_color') }}\"\n      # Up here because the turn-off lists below exclude idle lights. Empty\n      # means dark.\n      template_idle_brightness: !input idle_brightness_template\n      morning_idle_brightness: !input morning_idle_brightness\n      day_idle_brightness: !input day_idle_brightness\n      evening_idle_brightness: !input evening_idle_brightness\n      night_idle_brightness: !input night_idle_brightness\n      phase_idle_brightness: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_idle_brightness, 'Day': day_idle_brightness,\n                    'Evening': evening_idle_brightness, 'Night': night_idle_brightness} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase, 0) | int }}\n      # Same precedence as brightness_levels. Takes '50%' too, but no 'x'\n      # multiplier: idle calls send no brightness to scale.\n      template_idle_map: >\n        {% set t = template_idle_brightness %}\n        {% set percent = t is string and (t | trim) is match('^[0-9.]+ *%$') %}\n        {% if t is mapping %}\n          {{ t }}\n        {% elif percent or (t is not none and (t | string | trim) != '' and (t | float(-1)) >= 0) %}\n          {% set level = (t | trim) if percent else (t | float) %}\n          {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: level}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n          {{ ns.m }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ {} }}\n        {% endif %}\n      idle_brightness: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% if phase_idle_brightness %}\n          {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n            {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: phase_idle_brightness}) %}\n          {% endfor %}\n        {% endif %}\n        {{ dict(ns.m, **template_idle_map) }}\n      # Lights that stay lit when the room empties. A null level outranks an\n      # idle one. A string counts by its number, so '0%' isn't idle and an\n      # 'x' multiplier is no level.\n      idle_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(items=[]) %}\n        {% for e, level in idle_brightness.items() %}\n          {% set n = level %}\n          {% if level is string %}\n            {% set s = level | trim %}\n            {% set n = (s[:-1] | float(0)) if s.endswith('%') else (s | float(0)) %}\n          {% endif %}\n          {% if n and e in resolved_entities and e not in hands_off_entities\n                and e not in lux_blocked_entities %}\n            {% set ns.items = ns.items + [e] %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.items }}\n      # Minus hands-off lights. Only feeds the motion_off turn-off.\n      reachable_entities: >\n        {{ resolved_entities | reject('is_state', 'unavailable') | reject('is_state', 'unknown')\n           | reject('in', hands_off_entities) | list }}\n      turn_off_entities: >\n        {{ reachable_entities | reject('in', idle_entities) | list }}\n      # Every idle light has a level, so the idle calls need no brightness.\n      idle_levels: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(m={}) %}\n        {% for e in idle_entities %}\n          {% set ns.m = dict(ns.m, **{e: idle_brightness[e]}) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.m }}\n      # The room's working occupancy and motion sensors; only those picked by\n      # name with Sensors From Areas off. An unavailable or unknown sensor\n      # isn't one, so a room whose only sensor is dead counts as having none\n      # rather than as empty.\n      room_occupancy_entities: >\n        {% set sensors = (room_entities | select('match', '^binary_sensor\\\\.')\n             | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'occupancy') | list\n           + room_entities | select('match', '^binary_sensor\\\\.')\n             | select('is_state_attr', 'device_class', 'motion') | list)\n           | reject('is_state', ['unavailable', 'unknown']) | list %}\n        {{ sensors if use_area_sensors\n           else sensors | select('in', named_entities) | list }}\n      # No occupancy sensor on, or changed, within the Wait time. Hand-written\n      # because occupancy.is_not_detected's `for:` isn't reliable after a\n      # restart. Only `on` counts as occupied, so a sensor left unavailable\n      # can't hold the room on forever. True with no sensors, so callers also\n      # check room_occupancy_entities.\n      occupancy_clear_for_wait: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(all_clear=true) %}\n        {% for e in room_occupancy_entities %}\n          {% if is_state(e, 'on') or\n                (now() - states[e].last_changed).total_seconds() < (no_motion_wait | int) %}\n            {% set ns.all_clear = false %}\n          {% endif %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.all_clear }}\n      # Empty, with lights that stay dimly lit. Suppresses the curve while\n      # idle: an idle light being on makes `occupied`, and so allow_turn_on,\n      # true, which would ramp the nightlight straight back up.\n      room_is_idle: >\n        {{ idle_entities | length > 0\n           and room_occupancy_entities | length > 0\n           and occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\n      occupied: >\n        {# The room is in use if anything it runs is already on. #}\n        {{ resolved_entities | reject('in', hands_off_entities)\n           | select('is_state', 'on') | list | count > 0 }}\n      # THE gate for switching a light on: motion, a manual run, the room\n      # already in use, or the room getting dark enough while someone is in it\n      # (Lux Threshold, at the user's request). Only two things may switch a\n      # light on:\n      #\n      #   scene.turn_on / flare.apply_lighting - inside default:'s single\n      #     `if allow_turn_on` block.\n      #   flare.apply_lighting for idle brightness - gated on idle_entities and\n      #     occupancy_clear_for_wait instead.\n      #\n      # Lux Threshold narrows both: too_bright drops the off lights from each\n      # call and keeps the scene from activating.\n      #\n      # Anything new that can switch a light on needs one of those gates. The\n      # idle gate must stay narrower than allow_turn_on, and must not be gated\n      # on `occupied`, which an idle light makes true.\n      allow_turn_on: >\n        {{ manual_run\n           or trigger_id == 'motion_on'\n           or occupied\n           or (trigger_id == 'lux_dark'\n               and not too_bright\n               and room_occupancy_entities | length > 0 and not occupancy_clear_for_wait) }}\n      # Retried by self-heal. Excludes hands-off and idle lights.\n      entities_still_on: >\n        {{ resolved_entities | select('is_state', 'on')\n           | reject('in', hands_off_entities) | reject('in', idle_entities) | list }}\n      # The room's entities and every entity on each light's device, for\n      # scene-compatibility checks.\n      scope_entities: >\n        {% set ns = namespace(entities=room_entities) %}\n        {% for e in resolved_entities %}\n          {% set did = device_id(e) %}\n          {% set ns.entities = ns.entities + (device_entities(did) if did else [e]) %}\n        {% endfor %}\n        {{ ns.entities | unique | list }}\n      morning_scene: !input morning_scene\n      day_scene: !input day_scene\n      evening_scene: !input evening_scene\n      night_scene: !input night_scene\n      phase_scene: >\n        {% set m = {'Morning': morning_scene, 'Day': day_scene, 'Evening': evening_scene, 'Night': night_scene} %}\n        {{ m.get(phase) }}\n      # scene_template overrides when it returns a valid scene; a typo or missing\n      # scene counts as nothing. The entity_id shape check has to come first:\n      # states[] raises on a malformed string, aborting the whole run.\n      desired_scene: >\n        {% set candidate = (scene_template | trim) %}\n        {% if candidate and candidate is match('^[a-z0-9_]+\\\\.[a-z0-9_]+$') and states[candidate] is not none %}\n          {{ candidate }}\n        {% elif phase_scene and states[phase_scene] is not none %}\n          {{ phase_scene }}\n        {% else %}\n          {{ '' }}\n        {% endif %}\n      # Re-activating a scene every minute would stomp manual changes, so the\n      # tick never does.\n      scene_recheck_due: \"{{ trigger_id != 'tick' }}\"\n      # No scene until flare.compute_scene_coverage says otherwise, in default:.\n      scene_coverage: \"{{ {'scene_valid': false, 'covered_entities': []} }}\"\n  # Never checks occupancy: an already-on light should follow the curve\n  # regardless. allow_turn_on decides whether lights may come on.\n  #\n  # motion_on stops if there's nothing to do - nothing off and nothing\n  # idle. `idle_entities`, not `room_is_idle`, which is false once motion\n  # starts.\n  - alias: \"Stop a motion_on run with nothing to turn on\"\n    if:\n      - condition: template\n        alias: \"Triggered by motion_on\"\n        value_template: \"{{ trigger_id == 'motion_on' }}\"\n      - condition: template\n        alias: \"Nothing in the room is off, and nothing has an idle level\"\n        value_template: >-\n          {{ resolved_entities | map('states') | select('ne', 'on') | list | count == 0\n             and idle_entities | length == 0 }}\n    then:\n      - stop: \"Nothing to turn on\"\n  - choose:\n      # The cleared triggers' `for:` is per sensor, so they fire once each\n      # sensor's own Wait time is up, even if another saw motion since.\n      - alias: \"Motion timed out and the room is confirmed empty\"\n        conditions:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Triggered by motion_off\"\n            value_template: \"{{ trigger_id == 'motion_off' }}\"\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Every occupancy sensor has been clear for the full Wait time\"\n            value_template: \"{{ occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\"\n        sequence:\n          # flare.turn_off keeps them FLARE's, so they aren't read as overridden\n          # while idle lights keep the room lit.\n          - alias: \"Turn off the light(s)\"\n            action: flare.turn_off\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ turn_off_entities }}\"\n              transition: !input motion_off_transition\n          # Idle lights are dimmed instead. Does nothing with no idle brightness.\n          - alias: \"Leave the idle-brightness lights dimly lit\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"Room has idle-brightness lights to dim\"\n                value_template: \"{{ idle_entities | length > 0 }}\"\n            then:\n              - action: flare.apply_lighting\n                data:\n                  entities: \"{{ idle_entities }}\"\n                  brightness_levels: \"{{ idle_levels }}\"\n                  color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n                  rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n                  transition: !input motion_off_transition\n                  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n                  room_id: \"{{ room_id }}\"\n                  room_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n      # Self-heal: on a tick, with the room empty, retry turn-offs that didn't\n      # land. Exclusive of default:, which would work from the same stale list.\n      - alias: \"Self-heal: retry an earlier turn-off that didn't land\"\n        conditions:\n          # phase_change too: moving to a phase with no idle brightness leaves\n          # lights on that no longer read as idle.\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Triggered by the periodic tick or a phase change\"\n            value_template: \"{{ trigger_id in ['tick', 'phase_change'] }}\"\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Room has an occupancy sensor to reconcile against\"\n            value_template: \"{{ room_occupancy_entities | length > 0 }}\"\n          # Continuously clear for the full Wait time, so a sensor blip can't turn\n          # lights off.\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Occupancy has been clear for the full Wait time\"\n            value_template: \"{{ occupancy_clear_for_wait }}\"\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Something in the room is still on\"\n            value_template: \"{{ entities_still_on | length > 0 }}\"\n        sequence:\n          - alias: \"Self-heal: retry turning off lights left on with no occupancy\"\n            action: flare.turn_off\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ entities_still_on }}\"\n              transition: !input motion_off_transition\n    default:\n      - alias: \"Work out which lights the scene takes, if there is one\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"A scene is chosen\"\n            value_template: \"{{ desired_scene | length > 0 }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Compute scene coverage (FLARE)\"\n            action: flare.compute_scene_coverage\n            data:\n              scene_entity_id: \"{{ desired_scene }}\"\n              scope_entities: \"{{ scope_entities }}\"\n              target_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n            response_variable: scene_coverage\n      # The scene counts only if it exists and everything it covers is in\n      # scope; otherwise FLARE drives every light.\n      - variables:\n          scene_valid: \"{{ scene_coverage.scene_valid }}\"\n          # Lights handed off this run - to an active scene, or via a\n          # null/false level. They're never written, so their claims are\n          # released instead of going stale into \"overridden\". Lights only: a\n          # scene can set other domains, which hold no claims.\n          handed_off_entities: >\n            {{ ((scene_coverage.covered_entities if scene_valid else []) + hands_off_entities)\n               | select('match', 'light[.]') | unique | list }}\n          # No off-light filter: the step using it is already behind\n          # allow_turn_on. Off lights are dropped while the room is too\n          # bright, so the call updates the ones already on and leaves the\n          # rest dark.\n          target_entities: >\n            {{ (scene_coverage.uncovered_entities if scene_valid else resolved_entities)\n               | reject('in', lux_blocked_entities) | list }}\n      # Everything that can switch a light on is under this gate (see\n      # allow_turn_on). An empty room settles to its idle brightness, outside\n      # the gate. room_occupancy_entities is checked because a room with no\n      # sensors would otherwise always read as empty.\n      - alias: \"Settle an empty room to its idle brightness\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Room is idle, and the sensor has a colour target\"\n            value_template: \"{{ room_is_idle and color_temp_kelvin is not none }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Apply idle brightness (FLARE)\"\n            action: flare.apply_lighting\n            data:\n              entities: \"{{ idle_entities }}\"\n              brightness_levels: \"{{ idle_levels }}\"\n              color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n              rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n              transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n              prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n              room_id: \"{{ room_id }}\"\n              room_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n      - alias: \"Only motion, a manual run, or a room already in use may switch a light on\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"Allowed to turn on, and not already handled by the idle nightlight\"\n            # Stops the nightlight ramping itself back up (see room_is_idle).\n            value_template: \"{{ allow_turn_on and not room_is_idle }}\"\n        then:\n          - alias: \"Activate a scene, if one applies and is due a recheck\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"A scene applies and is due a recheck, and can't light a bright room\"\n                # Activating it sets every light it covers, so while it's too\n                # bright only once they're all on already. Its lights stay the\n                # scene's either way.\n                value_template: >\n                  {{ scene_valid and scene_recheck_due\n                     and (not too_bright\n                          or scene_coverage.covered_entities | select('match', 'light[.]')\n                             | reject('is_state', 'on') | list | count == 0) }}\n            then:\n              - alias: \"Activate matching scene\"\n                action: scene.turn_on\n                target:\n                  entity_id: \"{{ desired_scene }}\"\n                data:\n                  transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n          # Guarded because the sensor attributes render null when the sensor is\n          # unavailable, and apply_lighting requires both.\n          - alias: \"Apply adaptive lighting, unless the sensor has no target to apply\"\n            if:\n              - condition: template\n                alias: \"Sensor has a real brightness and colour target\"\n                value_template: \"{{ schedule_brightness is not none and color_temp_kelvin is not none }}\"\n            then:\n              - alias: \"Apply adaptive lighting (FLARE)\"\n                action: flare.apply_lighting\n                data:\n                  entities: \"{{ target_entities }}\"\n                  brightness_levels: \"{{ brightness_levels }}\"\n                  brightness: \"{{ schedule_brightness }}\"\n                  color_temp_kelvin: \"{{ color_temp_kelvin }}\"\n                  rgb_color: \"{{ rgb_color }}\"\n                  transition: \"{{ script_transition }}\"\n                  prefer_rgb_color: \"{{ prefer_rgb_color }}\"\n                  room_id: \"{{ room_id }}\"\n                  room_entities: \"{{ resolved_entities }}\"\n                  # A manual run forces the tick through override protection.\n                  force: \"{{ manual_run }}\"\n      # Bookkeeping only, so outside the gate.\n      - alias: \"Release lights handed off to a scene or another owner\"\n        if:\n          - condition: template\n            alias: \"There are lights to release, with override protection on\"\n            value_template: >-\n    